  "caption": "Quinn stubbed a toe and was sure it was the end. Five minutes later: fine. Then a scan report mentioning a \"disc bulge\" sent Quinn into an online spiral.\n\nPain is your nervous system's protective alarm, not a damage meter. Plenty of people with disc bulges on scans have no pain at all, and pain can be turned up by many things besides tissue damage.\n\nWhat can help: learning how pain works, returning to activity gradually, protecting your sleep, and looking after stress, since the whole person matters.\n\nGet it checked if pain is new, severe, worsening or has no clear cause.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
